runtimes: compiler-rt, libc++ and libc++abi on EmiBSD

Why a patch: the runtimes pick their platform code by predefined macro, and
__EmiBSD__ is new to them. Where they ask for the libc interfaces EmiBSD's libc
provides, EmiBSD joins the condition: <machine/endian.h>'s _BYTE_ORDER and
elf_aux_info(3) in compiler-rt's builtins; arc4random(3) for std::random_device,
the pthread API, the default rune table, the <sys/futex.h> futex(2) call and
clock_gettime(2) in libc++; the same futex in libc++abi's guard; and libc++ as the
default C++ library in compiler-rt's CMake. The libc++ locale layer for this libc
is the one upstream names openbsd.h; it is included, not copied.
Written by EmiBSD (ISC); carried by DevTools over the pinned tag. Author: Emilio
Navarrete Lineros, 2026-10-31.

